<title>GREECE: Greek CPI inflation falls to 8.3pct yr/yr in Oct.</title>
<headline>Greek CPI inflation falls to 8.3pct yr/yr in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek consumer price inflation dropped to 8.3 percent year-on-year in October from 8.5 percent in September, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said in a statement.</p>
<p>Greek bankers and economists polled by Reuters predicted that inflation would fall to 8.4 percent in October.</p>
<p> Consumer Price Index   October 96  September 96 October 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month		 0.9%	  3.0%	   1.1%</p>
<p> Rate of change		 8.3%	  8.5%	   8.3%</p>
<p> Index (1988=100)	   292.8	 290.1	  270.4</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
